  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n+1)\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\u2026,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=-\\pi .\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
